.TH DAVID 8 "November 2026" "david-server 0.1.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
david \- the David server: audiobook and music library of the family
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B david
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B david run
.RB [ \-\-data\-dir
.IR dir ]
.RB [ \-\-listen
.IR addr [, addr ...]]
.RB [ \-\-mcp ]
.RB [ \-\-no\-announce ]
.RB [ \-\-log
.IR level ]
.RB [ \-\-tls\-cert
.I file
.B \-\-tls\-key
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-\-tls\-host
.IR name ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B david
serves the audiobooks and the music of a household to the apps of the family (Psalm), with a web
administration, a Bible reader, podcasts, radio stations, playlists, the import of audio CDs from the
drive of the server and, if switched on, an MCP endpoint for a language model that looks after the tags.
.PP
The packaged service
.RB ( david.service )
runs
.B david run
as root. At the start the server reads
.BR /etc/david.toml ,
gives the service user the rights on the library folders (POSIX ACLs), joins the extra groups of the
file, hands the data folder to the service user and then drops to that user for good.
.PP
A value comes from, in this order: the command line, the environment, the file
.BR /etc/david.toml ,
the built\-in default. Everything that the family decides in the administration pages (import folders,
rules, the settings of the CD import, profiles and rights) lives in the database, not in the file.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B run
Run the server in the foreground until Ctrl\-C or SIGTERM. This is what the service starts.
.TP
.B init
Create the first administrator before the first start. The PIN or password is asked twice on a
terminal, or read as one line from standard input.
.B \-\-name
sets the name (default: Papa).
.TP
.B reset\-pin
Set a new PIN or password for a user who forgot it;
.BI \-\-name " NAME"
is required. The user is signed out everywhere and any lock is lifted.
.TP
.B reindex
Read the import folders again, like the switch \(lqSync now\(rq of the administration pages: new and
changed files are read, albums whose files are gone are taken out. Also
.BR "david \-\-reindex" .
Run every hour by
.BR david\-reindex.timer .
The import has to be unlocked.
.TP
.B prune
Only the tidying of
.BR reindex :
take the albums out of the library whose files are gone from the disk.
.B \-\-dry\-run
only lists them;
.B \-\-force
lifts the stop for a run that would remove more than a third of the albums (a disk that is not mounted
looks like that).
.TP
.B renew\-cert
Make a new server certificate with the current addresses and host name of this machine
.RB ( \-\-data\-dir ", " \-\-listen ).
The old one is kept as
.BR cert.pem.old .
Paired devices pin the certificate, so every device has to be paired again. Stop the server first.
.TP
.B export\-templates
Write the built\-in page templates and the stylesheet to
.BI \-\-to " DIR" ,
as a starting point for templates of one's own (see
.BR DAVID_TEMPLATES_DIR ).
.TP
.B version
Show the version, the git revision and the build time.
.TP
.B help
Show the usage.
.TP
.BR service ", " install ", " uninstall
Windows only: the entry point of the service manager, and registering or removing the Windows service.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-data\-dir " DIR"
The folder of the database
.RB ( david.db ),
the certificate
.RB ( tls/ )
and the staging area of the CD import. Default
.BR /var/lib/david .
.TP
.BI \-\-listen " ADDR" [, ADDR ...]
Where the interface listens, default
.BR 127.0.0.1:8484 .
Several addresses, separated by commas, are served at the same time, for example
.B 0.0.0.0:8484,[::]:8484
(IPv4 and IPv6 are separate addresses; the packaged service listens on both). Anything but this
machine speaks TLS, with a certificate the server makes itself unless
.B \-\-tls\-cert
is given; the pairing code of the apps carries its fingerprint.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-announce
Do not announce the server on the network (mDNS). The apps then find it only by its address.
.TP
.B \-\-mcp
Serve
.B /mcp
for a language model that looks at the library and corrects ID tags. Access needs a token made in the
settings (LLM access); what the token may do depends on the profile that made it.
.TP
.BI \-\-log " LEVEL"
.BR error ", " warn ", " info " (default), " debug " or " trace .
.B debug
is for David's own code; the libraries (the database queries) join in at
.BR trace .
Also a setting in the administration pages, where it changes at once.
.TP
.BI \-\-tls\-cert " FILE" "\fR,\fP \-\-tls\-key " FILE
A certificate (PEM, with its chain) from a certificate authority, for example Let's Encrypt, and its
private key, instead of the self\-made certificate. The service user has to be able to read both. A
renewed certificate is loaded without a restart.
.TP
.BI \-\-tls\-host " NAME"
The name that devices connect to with such a certificate: they then check the name, not a fingerprint,
and the pairing code carries the name.
.TP
.BI \-\-name " NAME"
The administrator for
.BR init ,
or the user for
.BR reset\-pin .
.TP
.BI \-\-to " DIR"
The target folder of
.BR export\-templates .
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
.BR prune :
only say what would be removed.
.TP
.B \-\-force
.BR prune :
also when many albums are gone.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B DAVID_CONFIG
The configuration file to read instead of
.BR /etc/david.toml .
.TP
.B DAVID_DATA_DIR
Like
.BR \-\-data\-dir .
.TP
.B DAVID_LISTEN
Like
.BR \-\-listen ,
addresses separated by commas.
.TP
.B DAVID_MCP
.B 1
is like
.BR \-\-mcp .
.TP
.B DAVID_LOG
Like
.BR \-\-log .
.TP
.BR DAVID_TLS_CERT ", " DAVID_TLS_KEY ", " DAVID_TLS_HOST
Like
.BR \-\-tls\-cert ", " \-\-tls\-key ", " \-\-tls\-host .
.TP
.B DAVID_TLS_RELOAD_S
How often, in seconds, a renewed certificate is looked for (default 300).
.TP
.B DAVID_FEATURE_DOWNLOAD
.BR 1 ", " true ", " yes " or " on
switches on the hidden download feature (administrators may take the original files of the library);
anything else switches it off, also against the file.
.TP
.B DAVID_TEMPLATES_DIR
A folder with page templates that replace the built\-in ones. Also looked up:
.BR /etc/david/templates ,
.BR /usr/share/david/templates .
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/david.toml
The settings of the machine; see
.BR david.toml (5).
.TP
.B /var/lib/david/david.db
The database: the library, the profiles, the settings of the pages, the logs.
.TP
.BR /var/lib/david/tls/cert.pem ", " key.pem
The self\-made certificate of the server and its key.
.TP
.B /var/lib/david/library
The default import folder of the package, owned by the service user.
.TP
.B /var/lib/david/cd\-import
The staging area of the CD import: rips under way, interrupted rips that can be continued (for
.B cd_resume_keep_hours
of the CD settings) and CDs that wait for approval.
.TP
.BR /usr/lib/systemd/system/david.service ", " david\-reindex.service ", " david\-reindex.timer
The service and the hourly
.BR reindex .
.TP
.B /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/61\-david\-cdrom.rules
Makes the kernel ask the CD drive only every 10 minutes whether the disc changed
.RB ( events_poll_msecs ),
because that question interrupts a rip. A new disc is then noticed late by the kernel; the server looks at
the drive itself every
.B cd_poll_seconds
while
.B cd_udev
is off in the CD settings. A file of the same name in
.B /etc/udev/rules.d
replaces it.
.SH SIGNALS
.TP
.BR SIGTERM ", " SIGINT
Stop. A CD that is being read finishes the track it is on if that takes no more than 10 seconds, writes
down what is finished and ends, so that the next start can continue it; the unit allows 60 seconds. A
rip that was under way waits after the start until a person chooses to read it again or to give it up;
it never goes on by itself.
.SH NOTES
The CD drive: the service user needs the group of the drive (usually
.BR cdrom )
in
.B groups
of
.BR /etc/david.toml .
A disc whose CD\-Text names the album, the performer and every track is filed under it, and MusicBrainz
is not asked for it; otherwise MusicBrainz is asked once a contact address is set in the CD settings.
.PP
Folders outside
.B /var/lib/david
need a drop\-in that opens them in the sandbox of the unit
.RB ( "systemctl edit david" ,
.BR ReadWritePaths= ;
.B ProtectHome=false
for folders below
.BR /home ).
Port 8484 must be open in the firewall for the apps.
.SH EXAMPLES
First start of the package:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sudo \-u david env DAVID_DATA_DIR=/var/lib/david /usr/bin/david init \-\-name Papa
sudo systemctl enable \-\-now david
.fi
.RE
.PP
Only on this machine, behind a reverse proxy:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sudo systemctl edit david
  [Service]
  Environment=DAVID_LISTEN=127.0.0.1:8484
.fi
.RE
.PP
See which albums a reindex would take out:
.PP
.RS
.nf
sudo \-u david env DAVID_DATA_DIR=/var/lib/david /usr/bin/david prune \-\-dry\-run
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR david.toml (5),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR systemd.exec (5),
.BR setfacl (1)
.PP
The FAQ and the specifications in the sources: https://github.com/Beerlesklopfer/Psalms\-Of\-David
